  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.95,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.07,
    "rationale": "The sudden plateau at about 0.96 after hourly doubling could have meant the reader was saturating, so I ran a dilution-linearity test on the late retained aliquots. 18 h: 10x dilution gave 0.094 and 0.0967 (mean 0.0953, which scales to 0.953). A 4x dilution gave 0.2334 (scales to 0.934). The undiluted reading was 0.9625. 16 h: 10x gave 0.096, scaling to 0.96 (undiluted 0.959). 14 h: 10x gave 0.1018, scaling to 1.02 (undiluted 0.955). That is about 6% higher, which fits single-replicate noise and is far from what saturation would produce. At two dilution factors and three late time points, the diluted readings scale back to the undiluted values within a few percent. If the reader were saturated, the diluted readings would scale back to much higher values. So the reader responds proportionally around OD 1, and the plateau is a real stationary phase. Late biomass is about OD600 0.95, as read."
  },
